{
  "dn19:0.1": "Long Discourses 19 ",
  "dn19:0.2": "The Great Steward ",
  "dn19:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn19:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "dn19:1.3": "Then, late at night, the centaur Pañcasikha, lighting up the entire Vulture’s Peak, went up to the Buddha, bowed, stood to one side, and said to him, ",
  "dn19:1.4": "“Sir, I would tell you of what I heard and learned directly from the gods of the thirty-three.” ",
  "dn19:1.5": "“Tell me, Pañcasikha,” said the Buddha. ",
  "dn19:2.0": "1. The Council of the Gods ",
  "dn19:2.1": "“Sir, it was more than a few days ago—on the fifteenth day sabbath on the full moon day at the invitation to admonish held at the end of the rainy season—when all the gods of the thirty-three were sitting together in the Hall of Clear Right. ",
  "dn19:2.2": "A large assembly of gods was sitting all around, and the four great kings were seated at the four quarters. ",
  "dn19:2.3": "The Great King Dhataraṭṭha was seated to the east, facing west, in front of his gods. ",
  "dn19:2.4": "The Great King Virūḷhaka was seated to the south, facing north, in front of his gods. ",
  "dn19:2.5": "The Great King Virūpakkha was seated to the west, facing east, in front of his gods. ",
  "dn19:2.6": "The Great King Vessavaṇa was seated to the north, facing south, in front of his gods. ",
  "dn19:2.7": "When the gods of the thirty-three have a gathering like this, that is how they are seated. ",
